+### `EXL3_DEC_GROUP` (default: `0`)
+
+Split-decode attention, graph-captured and eager: a program takes up to 32 of a kv head's
+(query position, GQA head) rows (`decode_row_layout`), so a verify step with more rows than that
+(q_len 8 with a group of 6 is 48) still reads and dequantizes each K/V tile in two programs. `1`
+raises the cap to 128 rows: one program per kv head while q_len x group <= 128 (every q_len up to
+16 for a group of 6 or 8; larger groups still split), and, unless
+`EXL3_DEC_SPLIT_MULT` is set, aims for 8 (single-token) or 4 (multi-token) programs per CU
+instead of 2. Tuned on gfx1201.
+
+### `EXL3_DEC_SPLIT_MULT` (default: unset)
+
+Programs per CU (a float) the split-decode split count aims for.
+
+### `EXL3_DEC_WARPS`, `EXL3_DEC_STAGES`, `EXL3_DEC_BLOCK_N` (default: unset)
+
+Override the split-decode kernel's warps, pipeline stages and kv tile (powers of two; stages
+non-negative) over the per-backend / per-architecture defaults (`attn_decode_config` in
+`exllamav3/util/backend.py`). Each applies on its own, in the eager launch and the
+graph-captured build alike; explicit arguments to `paged_attn_triton_decode` still win. A set
+`EXL3_DEC_BLOCK_N` replaces the shared-memory ladder with that one tile.
+
+### `EXL3_DEC_Q4W` (default: `0`)
+
+Word-sliced split-decode kernel for 4-bit K and V caches (head_dim a power of two, at least 128):
+each tile's packed words are loaded once and the dots split into 8 per-nibble partial dots,
+instead of unpacking through an LDS shuffle. 1.2-1.3x the packed kernel on gfx1201 at q_len 4-8.
+
 ### `EXL3_BC_ATTN_TRACE` (default: `0`)
 
 Print one line per attention module/cache-layer pair when the graph-captured decode path is
@@ -118,6 +146,13 @@ Gated-delta-net (Qwen3-Next/3.5, KDA in GLM-5.3/Kimi Linear) counterpart of `EXL
 the decode step of a linear-attention layer runs as one graph-captured C++ call. Set to `0` to
 force the torch path, for A/B testing.
 
+### `EXL3_BC_MLP_MAX_ROWS` (default: `32`)
+
+Most rows (bsz x q_len) the graphed dense GatedMLP path (`BC_GatedMLP`) takes; larger inputs run
+the eager path. The limit is 32 (`MLP_MAX_ROWS`, which also sizes the shared static scratch), so a
+batched speculative verify up to 4 x 8 rows stays graphed; `8` restores the previous limit.
+Read at import.
+
 ### `EXL3_GDN_SUB_CHUNK` (default: `2048`)
 
 Prefill of a gated-delta-net / KDA layer runs the fla chunked scan over consecutive sub-ranges
@@ -274,6 +309,28 @@ the path wherever its hard constraints allow (testing).
 Weight-extraction strategy inside the fp16 GEMV kernel: `-1` picks per bitrate (default), `0`
 forces shuffle extraction, `1` forces shared-memory staging. Testing only.
 
+### `EXL3_GEMV_WMMA` (ROCm gfx1200 / gfx1201; default: `0`)
+
+Multi-row EXL3 GEMV (2-32 rows, e.g. a speculative verify, or a batched one at bsz 4 x 8 rows) on
+the gfx12 WMMA units: each 16x16 trellis tile is decoded once and one `v_wmma_f32_16x16x16_f16`
+per 16 rows takes them all, instead of one fdot2 chain per row. Covers integer bitrates in the single-matrix
+GEMV and the unweighted single-token multi-matrix GEMV; everything else keeps the fdot2 kernels
+(2-8 rows) or the cooperative GEMM (9 rows and up). Devices other than
+gfx1200 / gfx1201 (gfx11 included) also keep them whatever the setting: eligibility is checked per
+device at runtime. Results match the fdot2 path to fp32 rounding, not bit for bit. Read on every
+call, unlike most C++-side variables, so tests can toggle it.
+
+### `EXL3_GEMV_MAX_M` (ROCm; default: `32`)
+
+Largest row count the RDNA multi-row GEMV takes (clamped to 1-32). Rows 9 and up need
+`EXL3_GEMV_WMMA` on a gfx12 device and fall back to the cooperative GEMM otherwise. `8` restores
+the original limit, `16` the single-M-tile one, `1` switches the multi-row path off. Read on every
+call.
+
+### `EXL3_GEMV_WMMA_U` (default: `4`)
+
+k-tiles decoded per WMMA batch in the `EXL3_GEMV_WMMA` kernel: `1`, `2` or `4`.
+
 ### `EXL3_INT8_GEMV` (default: `2`)
 
 Fused int8-activation GEMV for tensors quantized with the mul1 codebook: one cooperative launch
